                <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b style='font-size:20px;color:#0D47A1'&gt;Solenoid via Dual-MOSFET Trigger Module — REPLACE DEAD MODULE (ECO-004 Rev G)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#555;font-size:12px'&gt;SIG on BCM 16/PR.05/T36 · D4184-class, trigger 3.3–20V · GOODRIG 12V 2A valve · 1N5408 flyback · 10kΩ gate pull-down (keep) · &lt;b style='color:#B71C1C'&gt;NEW: 3A fuse on 12V feed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;fontColor=#333;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="330" y="18" width="840" height="52" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="fault_banner" value="&lt;b style='color:#FFFFFF;font-size:11px'&gt;⚠ 2026-07-04 FAULT: OUT+ ↔ OUT− = 9 Ω (healthy = open) → MOSFETs failed SHORT. REPLACE MODULE.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#FFCDD2;font-size:9px'&gt;A shorted FET conducts with no gate signal → solenoid energized at power-on, chattered, rail sagged → Jetson browned out. The 10k pull-down did NOT fail — it can't switch off a blown transistor. Pull-down + flyback stay.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#C62828;strokeColor=#B71C1C;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=4;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="330" y="74" width="550" height="70" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
