                <mxCell id="fuse" value="&lt;b style='color:#B71C1C;font-size:9px'&gt;3A fuse&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFEBEE;strokeColor=#B71C1C;strokeWidth=2;arcSize=40;fontColor=#B71C1C;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="358" y="322" width="56" height="22" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_12_l" value="&lt;b style='font-size:10px;color:#C62828'&gt;★ NEW: +12V → 3A inline fuse → DC IN +&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="278" y="350" width="220" height="16" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_jetson_gnd" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#424242;strokeWidth=3;rounded=1;" parent="1" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="150" y="296" as="sourcePoint"/>
                        <mxPoint x="150" y="600" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_dcin_gnd" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#424242;strokeWidth=3;rounded=1;" parent="1" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="502" y="396" as="sourcePoint"/>
                        <mxPoint x="502" y="600" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_dcin_gnd_l" value="&lt;b style='font-size:9px;color:#555'&gt;DC IN − → GND bus&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="506" y="500" width="130" height="16" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_outp" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#E53935;strokeWidth=4;rounded=1;" parent="1" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="864" y="332" as="sourcePoint"/>
                        <mxPoint x="980" y="345" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_outp_l" value="&lt;b style='font-size:10px;color:#C62828'&gt;OUT + → solenoid (+)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="878" y="306" width="150" height="18" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_outn" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#1E88E5;strokeWidth=4;rounded=1;dashed=1;" parent="1" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="864" y="384" as="sourcePoint"/>
                        <mxPoint x="980" y="400" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_outn_l" value="&lt;b style='font-size:10px;color:#1565C0'&gt;★ OUT − → solenoid (−)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="876" y="404" width="160" height="18" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="gndbus" value="" style="rounded=1;fillColor=#212121;strokeColor=#616161;shadow=1;arcSize=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="600" width="1160" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="gndbusl" value="&lt;b style='color:#E0E0E0;font-size:12px'&gt;COMMON GND BUS — Jetson GND + 12V PSU GND + module GND (header GND &amp; DC IN −) + Wago #2 (pull-down)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="604" width="1160" height="22" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="pd_callout" value="&lt;b style='color:#BF360C;font-size:12px'&gt;WHY THE 10kΩ PULL-DOWN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#5D4037;font-size:10px'&gt;At boot (power-on → app claims PR.05, ~30–60s) the Jetson pad floats to ~2.8V. That half-turns the logic-level MOSFET ON: solenoid energizes, MOSFET sits in its linear region and &lt;b&gt;runs hot&lt;/b&gt;, LED glows dim/flickers. The 10kΩ from GATE→GND pins the gate to 0V whenever the Jetson isn't actively driving 3.3V HIGH → MOSFET OFF, valve CLOSED at boot / reset / crash / wire-off.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF3E0;strokeColor=#BF360C;fontColor=#333;fontSize=10;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="900" y="70" width="330" height="120" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px;color:#B71C1C'&gt;Step-by-step (Rev G): swap in a NEW module — move these wires, in this order&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;0. EVERYTHING OFF:&lt;/b&gt; Jetson off, 12V adapter unplugged, solenoid spade connectors pulled off.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Confirm the old module is dead:&lt;/b&gt; meter across old &lt;b&gt;OUT+ ↔ OUT−&lt;/b&gt; = ~9 Ω (short). A good module reads open/OL. Bin the old module. Take a fresh one from the 5-pack.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Move each wire FROM the dead module TO the same-named terminal on the NEW module (nothing changes at the Jetson, Wagos, or solenoid ends):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt; Jumper from &lt;b&gt;Wago #1&lt;/b&gt; (gate node) → new module &lt;b&gt;SIG / PWM&lt;/b&gt; header pin.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt; Jumper from &lt;b&gt;Wago #2&lt;/b&gt; (GND node) → new module &lt;b&gt;GND&lt;/b&gt; header pin. (&lt;b&gt;VCC pin stays open&lt;/b&gt; — LED only.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt; +12V feed → new module &lt;b&gt;DC IN +&lt;/b&gt; screw. &lt;b&gt;★ NEW: put a 3A inline fuse in this wire&lt;/b&gt; — if a MOSFET ever shorts again, the fuse blows instead of dragging the shared 12V rail (and the Jetson) down.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5.&lt;/b&gt; 12V supply negative (GND bus) → new module &lt;b&gt;DC IN −&lt;/b&gt; screw. &lt;b&gt;Check polarity twice&lt;/b&gt; — reversed DC IN killed an adapter before.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6.&lt;/b&gt; Solenoid &lt;b&gt;RED (+) → OUT +&lt;/b&gt; screw · Solenoid &lt;b&gt;BLUE (−) → OUT −&lt;/b&gt; screw. &lt;b&gt;1N5408 flyback stays on the solenoid&lt;/b&gt; (band → + side).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;Do NOT touch&lt;/b&gt; the 10kΩ pull-down or the Wagos — that part is correct and still required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style='color:#1B5E20'&gt;Power-up verification (solenoid still DISCONNECTED):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V1.&lt;/b&gt; Meter checks first: new &lt;b&gt;OUT+ ↔ OUT−&lt;/b&gt; = open ✓ · &lt;b&gt;SIG → GND&lt;/b&gt; ≈ 10kΩ ✓ · &lt;b&gt;DC IN+ ↔ DC IN−&lt;/b&gt; ≠ 0 Ω ✓.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V2.&lt;/b&gt; Unplug the Jetson&#39;s DC pigtail from the shared 12V split, then apply 12V to the module only: LED must stay &lt;b&gt;OFF&lt;/b&gt; (the 10k pull-down holds SIG at 0V). LED ON with SIG at 0V = stop — bad module or SIG mis-wired.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V3.&lt;/b&gt; Cold-boot the Jetson: &lt;b&gt;SIG → GND must stay ~0V the entire boot&lt;/b&gt;, LED OFF.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V4.&lt;/b&gt; Run the dashboard click test — LED flashes, &lt;b&gt;OUT+ ↔ OUT−&lt;/b&gt; switches 12V↔0V. Only now power off and reconnect the solenoid.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#5D4037'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Recommended (commercial robustness):&lt;/b&gt; give the Jetson its own supply, separate from the solenoid 12V — a valve/driver fault must never brown out the flight computer. Until then, the 3A fuse is the minimum protection.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#1976D2;fontColor=#333;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="650" width="1160" height="400" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="2" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=http://www.haoyuelectronics.com/Attachment/MOSFET-Trigger-Switch-Module/MOSFET-Trigger-Switch-Module-7.jpg;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="150" width="220" height="182" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>